1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:03,093
Chapter 8. Thirteen years.

2
00:00:03,393 --> 00:00:09,280
In 2017, the Nintendo Switch erased the line between home console and handheld.

3
00:00:09,460 --> 00:00:15,875
It has sold over 157 million units: less than three million away from catching the PlayStation 2.

4
00:00:16,055 --> 00:00:25,640
Its successor, the Switch 2, sold 3.5 million in its first four days. No Nintendo console had ever launched that fast.

5
00:00:25,820 --> 00:00:32,311
In 2025, the industry surpassed $200 billion for the first time.

6
00:00:32,491 --> 00:00:39,585
And meanwhile, GTA V never stopped selling: over 230 million copies.

7
00:00:39,765 --> 00:00:44,444
Its successor was announced. Delayed once. And again.

8
00:00:44,624 --> 00:00:51,115
Now it has a date: November 19, 2026. Thirteen years later.

9
00:00:51,765 --> 00:01:00,218
It all started with a dot of light on a five-inch screen, so lab visitors don't get bored. Today, it is an entire city.

10
00:01:01,118 --> 00:01:04,891
And the next chapter of this story… is about to begin.
